  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grant Maritime and Port</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project contains of several developmental activities in the ports of San Pedro and Abidjan in C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire to be executed in 2023. These activities entail the continuation of the partnership Port of Amsterdam International (PoAI) has fostered over the preceding years with the respective port authorities of Port Autonome de San Pedro (PASP) and Port Autonome d&#x2019;Abidjan (PAA). As such, they seek to build on the projects that have already been carried out by PoAI in collaboration with the PASP and the PAA, as well as projects currently ongoing.The project will increase the sustainability, efficiency and effectiveness of the PAA and PASP. This will lead to improvement of the local business climate, and improve the performance of the logistical chain, which will create immediate advantages for the competitive position of the PAA and PASP in the region of West Africa.This increased performance will benefit the economic development of C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire and its hinterland as the PAA serves as port for the hinterland (Sahel countries). Furthermore, by creating a sustainability policy for the PASP the port of San Pedro would be a more attractive partner for international and national stakeholders, thus increasing the port value.</narrative>
  </description>
